2.32.5 change https://github.com/psf/requests/commit/90fee0876aea97c639b3bf698d83a12876d2f160 breaks passing of custom ssl context using an adapter like this:

```python3
class SSLContextAdapter(requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter):
    @override
    def init_poolmanager(self, *args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:
        kwargs["ssl_context"] = ssl.create_default_context()
        return super().init_poolmanager(*args, **kwargs)  # type: ignore

ssl_adapter = SSLContextAdapter()
session.mount("https://", ssl_adapter)
```

Now, if `verify=True`, the code in https://github.com/psf/requests/blob/90fee0876aea97c639b3bf698d83a12876d2f160/src/requests/adapters.py#L292-L313 always sets `ca_certs`, which causes urllib3 to modify the ssl_context by [loading more certs into it here](https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/blob/3d934808397b9cee14c6f399a4e6c9ddeb17a00d/src/urllib3/util/ssl_.py#L456-L460).

EDIT: I can be fixed by overriding also `cert_verify`:

```python3
class SSLContextAdapter(requests.adapters.HTTPAdapter):
